BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:casa-de-velazquez-artists-in-residence-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261105T001523Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261127T113000Z
DTEND:20261127T120000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 13:00 CET: Casa de Velazquez: Artists in Residence 2027-20
 28 (Academie de France a Madrid)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 27 Nov 2026 at 13:00 CET.\n\nThe Academie de France a Ma
 drid at the Casa de Velazquez offers 12 one-year residencies for 2027-2028
  to young graduates and established artists developing a creative project 
 in the Iberian Peninsula.\n\nOrganisation: Casa de Velazquez\, Academie de
  France a Madrid\nLocation: Madrid\, Spain (residence at the Casa de Velaz
 quez). No nationality requirement\, but EU/Schengen nationals must be affi
 liated to an artist/author or self-employed scheme in their country of res
 idence\, and non-EU applicants need a French residence permit allowing wor
 k or a Schengen work and residence permit from another EU state. Good Fren
 ch required.\nAward: Monthly residency grant voted each year\; for 2026-20
 27 it was EUR 3\,600 per month for artists housed at the Casa and EUR 4\,6
 00 per month for artists living outside (with children). Twelve monthly pa
 yments\, September 2027 to August 2028. Housing and studio provided\; a pr
 oduction support fund is also available on project. No application fee.\nD
 uration: 12 months (1 September 2027 to 31 August 2028\; on site mid-Septe
 mber to about 20 July)\n\nMore: https://www.casadevelazquez.org/que-pasa-e
 n-la-casa/detail/appel-artistes-en-residence-2027-2028?utm_source=artifici
 alnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.casadevelazquez.org/que-pasa-en-la-casa/detail/appel-artist
 es-en-residence-2027-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Madrid\, Spain (residence at the Casa de Velazquez). No nationalit
 y requirement\, but EU/Schengen nationals must be affiliated to an artist/
 author or self-employed scheme in their country of residence\, and non-EU 
 applicants need a French residence permit allowing work or a Schengen work
  and residence permit from another EU state. Good French required.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:effea-call-5-festival-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261105T001523Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: EFFEA Call #5: European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artis
 ts
DESCRIPTION:The European Festivals Fund for Emerging Artists (EFFEA)\, an i
 nitiative of the European Festivals Association co-funded by the European 
 Union\, opens its fifth call: 50 residencies for 50 emerging artists (indi
 viduals\, groups or collectives) hosted by partnerships of around 150 fest
 ivals\, each led by one leading festival with a minimum of two partner fes
 tivals from different eligible countries.\n\nOrganisation: European Festiv
 als Association (EFA)\nLocation: Residencies hosted by festival partnershi
 ps of at least three festivals from three eligible countries (most of Euro
 pe plus Tunisia and Ukraine). Leading festivals and artists must be based 
 in an eligible country\; festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\,
  Turkey and the UK may join as partner festivals only\, and artists from t
 hose countries may also be proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing the
  artists\; artists cannot apply directly.\nAward: 50 residency grants: 40 
 Discovery grants of EUR 8\,000 (for artists at an early career stage) and 
 10 Springboard grants of EUR 15\,000 (for artists established at home and 
 ready to break through internationally). A minimum of 80 percent of the gr
 ant must cover costs incurred by the artists (fees\, travel\, accommodatio
 n\, subsistence). An own contribution of EUR 1\,000 (Discovery) or EUR 2\,
 000 (Springboard) is deducted from the paid grant. No application fee.\nDu
 ration: Residencies implemented between 1 January and 31 December 2027\, c
 o-produced by one leading festival and at least two partner festivals\n\nM
 ore: https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.effea.eu/application-form?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residencies hosted by festival partnerships of at least three fest
 ivals from three eligible countries (most of Europe plus Tunisia and Ukrai
 ne). Leading festivals and artists must be based in an eligible country\; 
 festivals from Israel\, Palestine\, Switzerland\, Turkey and the UK may jo
 in as partner festivals only\, and artists from those countries may also b
 e proposed. Note: festivals apply\, proposing the artists\; artists cannot
  apply directly.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:emap-emare-media-art-residencies-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261105T001523Z
