SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: EHIN European Hybrid Intelligence Network: Dirt
 y Lab Artist Residencies in Biocomputing (2027)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 04 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nEHIN invites artists to exp
 lore hybrid intelligence through the shared agency of the more-than-human 
 world: biocomputing\, interspecies and multi-species communication\, biofa
 brication\, sensing and biohybrid systems\, building new artistic narrativ
 es rooted in ecological knowledge.\n\nOrganisation: European Hybrid Intell
 igence Network (Kersnikova\, ZKM\, Kontejner\, LABoral\, CPN\, GLUON)\, co
 -funded by Creative Europe\nLocation: Six host labs: Kersnikova (Ljubljana
 )\, ZKM (Karlsruhe)\, Kontejner (Zagreb)\, LABoral (Gijon)\, CPN (Belgrade
 )\, GLUON (Brussels\, with Utrecht). Applicants must be residents or taxpa
 yers in the EU or an eligible non-EU country.\nAward: EUR 25\,000 fixed re
 sidency grant per artist (6 artists)\, covering fee (max 35%) and producti
 on\; travel and accommodation arranged separately with the host\; optional
  extra co-production budget in Phase 2. No application fee.\nDuration: Abo
 ut 12 months: Phase 1 February to September 2027 on site\, Phase 2 October
  2027 to January 2028 co-production\n\nMore: https://europeanhybridintelli
 gencenetwork.eu/open-call/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:https://europeanhybridintelligencenetwork.eu/open-call/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Six host labs: Kersnikova (Ljubljana)\, ZKM (Karlsruhe)\, Kontejne
 r (Zagreb)\, LABoral (Gijon)\, CPN (Belgrade)\, GLUON (Brussels\, with Utr
 echt). Applicants must be residents or taxpayers in the EU or an eligible 
 non-EU country.
END:VEVENT
